<p>In the latest development, Israel said Iran launched missiles at the country on April 2, shortly after President Donald Trump delivered a White House speech on the war. Israeli authorities reported incoming fire as the wider U.S.-Israeli conflict with Iran continued. The sequence underscored how quickly political signaling and military action are feeding into each other in an already volatile confrontation. RFE/RL and Al-Monitor described the fighting as ongoing, with no clear immediate sign of de-escalation even as Trump said the campaign was nearing its end.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Domestic audience: Al-Monitor said Trump used the White House speech to reassure war-weary Americans, suggesting the address was aimed at public sentiment at home as well as at Iran.</li><li>Escalation language: Al-Monitor reported that Trump threatened to bomb Iran into the “Stone Ages,” sharpening his earlier promise of “extremely hard” strikes.</li><li>Threat horizon: Al-Monitor said the heavy strikes Trump mentioned could come in the next two to three weeks, putting a concrete near-term window on possible escalation.</li><li>Regional strain: RFE/RL said the war continues to shape the region, pointing to effects that go beyond a single missile exchange.</li></ul><blockquote>Thanks to the progress we&#x27;ve made, I can say tonight that we are on track to complete all of America&#x27;s military objectives shortly, very shortly - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli authorities: Israel’s account centered on incoming missile fire, emphasizing the real-time nature of the attack. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-protests-live-blog-trump-khamenei/33640284.html'>RFE/RL</a>)</li><li>Iranian military: Iran’s military framed its threatened response as a direct answer to President Trump’s threats, linking its public stance to U.S. pressure as well as to Israel. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/donald-trump-addresses-nation-on-iran-israel-war-live-updates-world-news/article70813995.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump: Trump cast the White House address as both an update on the campaign and a warning that more U.S. strikes could follow. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/iran-fires-missiles-israel-after-trump-threatens-weeks-strikes'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-protests-live-blog-trump-khamenei/33640284.html'>Israel Reports Missile Attacks From Iran</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/donald-trump-addresses-nation-on-iran-israel-war-live-updates-world-news/article70813995.ece'>Iran-Israel war LIVE: Israel reports Iranian missile attacks after Trump’s speech</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/iran-fires-missiles-israel-after-trump-threatens-weeks-strikes'>Iran fires missiles at Israel after Trump threatens weeks of strikes</a> - al-monitor.com</li></ul>